.TH VCVPLUGIN-INSTALL 1 2026-10-16 "vcvplugin-installer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vcvplugin-install \- inspect, compare and install VCV Rack 2 plugin packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vcvplugin-install
.RI [ options ]
.IR PACKAGE .vcvplugin " ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
VCV Rack unpacks
.I .vcvplugin
packages from its plugins folder the next time it starts, without saying what changed.
.B vcvplugin-install
checks each package first, reports what installing it will do, and unpacks it right away.
.PP
A package is rejected when it is built for another operating system or CPU, or has no valid
.IR plugin.json .
Each accepted package is reported as a new install, an upgrade, a downgrade, or the version already installed.
Downgrades, same-version packages with different files, and other warnings need confirmation; see
.B \-\-yes
and
.BR \-\-interactive .
.PP
Plugins are unpacked into a staging folder and then swapped into place, so an interrupted install leaves no
half-written plugin. Older packages for the same plugin that are still waiting for Rack to unpack them are removed,
so Rack does not unpack them over the new install.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Proceed past warnings (downgrades, same-version rebuilds, ...).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Ask before proceeding past warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-reinstall
Install even when the identical version is already installed.
.TP
.B \-\-defer
Copy the package for Rack to unpack on its next start instead of unpacking now.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Only report what would happen.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only report problems.
.TP
.B \-\-wait
Wait for Enter before exiting, for terminal launchers.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every package was installed, or was already installed.
.TP
.B 1
Some package failed to install or was rejected.
.TP
.B 2
Some package was skipped because it needs confirmation.
.TP
.B 3
Both 1 and 2.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RACK_USER_DIR
Rack's user folder; plugins are installed into its
.I plugins\-lin\-x64
folder. Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/Rack2 .
.TP
.B RACK_EXECUTABLE
The Rack executable started by the GUI's
.I Start Rack2
button. Default: the first of
.B Rack
on
.BR PATH ,
.IR ~/Rack2*/Rack ,
.IR ~/Applications/Rack2*/Rack ,
.IR ~/.local/opt/Rack2*/Rack " and"
.IR /opt/Rack2*/Rack .
.SH EXAMPLES
Install a downloaded plugin, asking before a downgrade:
.PP
.RS
.B vcvplugin-install \-i ~/Downloads/Fundamental-2.6.4-lin-x64.vcvplugin
.RE
.PP
See what installing every package in a folder would do:
.PP
.RS
.B vcvplugin-install \-n ~/Downloads/*.vcvplugin
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.B vcvplugin-gui
is the graphical installer, which opens
.I .vcvplugin
files from the file manager.
.PP
https://github.com/un1tz3r0/vcvplugin-installer
